From 8acbae73cc3abd899e388b21c2a06a98b47ca31d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 13:54:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] security review: one bar for ticked rows, the watch rules as
 a list; /jffs/nvram write-for-everyone healed

The review card had a button per row and kept the watch rules in a raw text
box. Now one bar acts on the ticked rows (accept, ignore, size and date
only), and the rules show as a list with Delete, Delete selected, Delete all
and an Add form (a new rule goes first; the first matching rule wins); the
text box stays behind Edit as text.

ASUS's prebuilt device discovery rewrites a JFFS-backed setting with
write-for-everyone set after the boot sweep cleared it, so the review and the
dashboard flagged it for good. Each watchdog tick now takes the bit off
/jffs/nvram files that carry it - only those, so an unchanged file is never
touched - before the review looks, with one log line per boot.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
